WEBVTT

00:00:05.849 --> 00:00:11.449
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday the seventeenth. Can you hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:13.439 --> 00:00:17.289
<v Callum Reid>We can hear you. Bit tinny, but that's probably the portakabin.</v>

00:00:19.429 --> 00:00:26.780
<v Sarah Okafor>The heating in the portakabin is ridiculous. Freezing when you get in, then tropical by the time you've made a brew.</v>

00:00:27.339 --> 00:00:31.190
<v Jamie Brennan>Good for drying your coat, though. About its only useful setting.</v>

00:00:32.859 --> 00:00:37.060
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyway, the football last night. Honestly, ninety minutes I'm not getting back.</v>

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.789
<v David Whitfield>You say that every week and still watch it.</v>

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.700
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, well. Apparently I enjoy being disappointed.</v>

00:00:46.909 --> 00:00:52.859
<v Callum Reid>I've got camping booked for the weekend. Looking at the weather, I'll be joining you on that.</v>

00:00:53.979 --> 00:00:55.380
<v Tomasz Nowak>Camping? This weekend? Brave.</v>

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.740
<v Callum Reid>That's the polite word for it. Forecast's basically sideways rain.</v>

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.359
<v Priya Raman>Lovely. A wet tent and no decent kettle.</v>

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:10.209
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes the holiday complaints line, let's do the board.</v>

00:01:10.689 --> 00:01:17.689
<v Sarah Okafor>First, I've already swapped the filter on the Injection Moulding Line 2 yesterday. That's finished, not another job for today.</v>

00:01:19.939 --> 00:01:24.140
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, that was still showing on my old view. That explains it.</v>

00:01:26.629 --> 00:01:33.980
<v Jamie Brennan>And I signed off the inspection on the Line 2 Pick and Place Robot on Tuesday. That one's closed as well.</v>

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.799
<v David Whitfield>Right, so neither of those is outstanding. Good.</v>

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:46.650
<v Sarah Okafor>Olumide, can you replace the seals on the booster pump by Monday? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:01:48.769 --> 00:01:54.019
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll replace the seals on the booster pump by Monday. Understood, that comes first.</v>

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:59.709
<v Callum Reid>Definitely the one hurting us. We're not getting round that production hold.</v>

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:06.260
<v David Whitfield>Just so we're clear, it's the seals we're talking about, not a whole pump replacement?</v>

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:11.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, the seals on the booster pump. Olumide has that, Monday, first priority.</v>

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.300
<v Olumide Adeyemi>That's clear. I've got it.</v>

00:02:16.419 --> 00:02:25.169
<v Tomasz Nowak>While we're on noises and pumps—well, not a pump actually. I heard a slight rattle from the CT1. Nothing to action yet, just an observation.</v>

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.289
<v David Whitfield>A slight rattle, rather than a proper knock?</v>

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:33.530
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, slight. I'm not raising a job off it.</v>

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:38.050
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Observation only, not adding that to today's work.</v>

00:02:38.689 --> 00:02:45.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Priya Raman, can you go to Northfield to pick up the replacement parts for the air dryer? That's fairly important.</v>

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:51.370
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I'll go to Northfield to pick up the replacement parts for the air dryer.</v>

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:56.280
<v Jamie Brennan>Sorry, you clipped out for me. Northfield?</v>

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:00.930
<v Priya Raman>Northfield, yes. The replacement parts for the air dryer.</v>

00:03:01.669 --> 00:03:05.520
<v Callum Reid>Not another full dryer, then. I heard about half that sentence.</v>

00:03:06.449 --> 00:03:10.300
<v Priya Raman>No, just the parts. Teams is doing its underwater thing again.</v>

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:18.280
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Priya Raman has the collection. Fairly important, but the booster pump remains the first job.</v>

00:03:19.909 --> 00:03:21.659
<v Jamie Brennan>Got you. Audio's back now.</v>

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:30.169
<v Tomasz Nowak>Um, I'll update the risk assessment for work on the Site Water System after lunch. That's fairly important.</v>

00:03:32.409 --> 00:03:36.259
<v David Whitfield>The assessment for the work, rather than changing the actual scope?</v>

00:03:36.719 --> 00:03:39.870
<v Tomasz Nowak>Exactly, the risk assessment. That's what I'm taking on.</v>

00:03:40.389 --> 00:03:45.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Tomasz Nowak. Risk assessment for work on the Site Water System, after lunch, fairly important.</v>

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:47.879
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, agreed.</v>

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:54.069
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Can I just get the parts blocker in before we move off water?</v>

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:55.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, go on.</v>

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:07.349
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Still waiting on parts for the feedwater pump, nothing we can do until they arrive. The repair's still blocked; I'm not taking that as a new job today.</v>

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.680
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, no arrival to report from stores. Still waiting.</v>

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:21.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood on the repair. Separately, I'll inspect the feedwater pump for leaks today at 2pm. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:23.639 --> 00:04:28.189
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Just the inspection, Sarah? Not trying to do the repair without the bits?</v>

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:34.230
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. I'll inspect it for leaks, that's all. The parts blocker stays against the repair.</v>

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:39.920
<v David Whitfield>Right, those are separate things. Looking for leaks doesn't mean we've magically got the parts.</v>

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.949
<v Callum Reid>If only saying it on Teams made them appear.</v>

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:49.089
<v Jamie Brennan>I'd have a much easier life, wouldn't I?</v>

00:04:49.759 --> 00:04:54.660
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll run a function test on the fire panel this afternoon. Normal priority.</v>

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:59.370
<v Priya Raman>That's yours then, Saz? The fire panel function test?</v>

00:05:00.089 --> 00:05:02.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, mine. This afternoon, normal priority.</v>

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:09.009
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, I spoke over you there. I thought you'd said that was at two as well.</v>

00:05:11.329 --> 00:05:20.430
<v Sarah Okafor>No, today at 2pm is my feedwater pump leak inspection. The fire panel function test is this afternoon; I haven't put a particular time on that.</v>

00:05:21.959 --> 00:05:24.410
<v Callum Reid>Ah, right. Two different entries. With you.</v>

00:05:25.449 --> 00:05:30.000
<v David Whitfield>And the parts wait doesn't change the leak inspection. All makes sense now.</v>

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:38.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. The two finished items stay closed, CT1 is just an observation, and the feedwater pump repair stays blocked.</v>

00:05:40.819 --> 00:05:45.019
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep. Nothing in that changes the booster pump being first for me.</v>

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:48.050
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. That's the lot, then. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:05:49.839 --> 00:05:51.589
<v Callum Reid>Cheers. Enjoy the tropical portakabin.</v>
